          "sourceKey": "mcc-issued-pws-text",
          "locator": "word/document.xml B053; PWS 2.2",
          "excerpt": "MCC is currently standardized on Microsoft solutions wherever applicable, and the agency is 95% Cloud based. OCIO continues to prioritize the enhanced utilization of Cloud technologies and investments to further utilize its AWS and Office 365 (O365) Cloud capabilities. "
        },
        {
          "sourceKey": "mcc-issued-pws-text",
          "locator": "word/document.xml B067; PWS 2.3",
          "excerpt": "Cost Effective: MCC requires an award structure that allows flexible adjustment of service levels and support based upon changes in the federal budget and evolving agency priorities. The Contractor must be able to tailor service levels, provide modular options that can scale up or down as needed, and maintain a flexible environment that accommodates emerging technologies and shifting business needs.  MCC also seeks a partner capable of building and sustaining cloud-based applications while efficiently managing both operations and maintenance (O&M) and new feature development to achieve cost savings. "
        },
        {
          "sourceKey": "mcc-issued-pws-text",
          "locator": "word/document.xml B160; PWS 4.2.2",
          "excerpt": "The Contractor shall provide support services for all applications and services within the Digital Services portfolio. Access to environments will be provided, but changes to production go through a change control process and are executed by another vendor or through OCIO’s CI/CD pipeline. SharePoint, ServiceNow and Box.com are exceptions, with elevated permissions provided to the Contractor/"
        },
        {
          "sourceKey": "mcc-issued-pws-text",
          "locator": "word/document.xml B265; PWS 4.2.2.3",
          "excerpt": "Additionally, the Contractor shall develop new applications that support MCC business requirements and operate within MCC's infrastructure specifications, policies, and guidance. Any commercial database packages utilized to develop data sets shall comply with MCC standards. The Contractor shall develop normalized data sets, apply maintenance of data sets (for creation, change, or deletion of records), and provide the necessary interfaces to link these data sets into an Intranet/Internet capable environment. The Contractor may use 'middleware' commercial packages consistent with MCC standards to integrate data sets for the purposes of collecting data, integrating with web pages, or providing data set files or services. Middleware must be proposed and agreed to by the Government to ensure that it meets information security standards and that out year maintenance and support are budgeted."
        },
        {
          "sourceKey": "mcc-issued-pws-text",
          "locator": "word/document.xml B267; PWS 4.2.2.3.1",
          "excerpt": "The Contractor shall develop customized applications utilizing the programming languages identified in Appendix B of this document or other programming languages (as necessary). All solutions must be responsive for desktops and mobile devices.  The Contractor shall have experience with mobile application development and mobile security, utilizing industry standard protocols and practices. The mobile applications will support multiple mobile OS platforms including Android and Apple. The Contractor may also be tasked with migrating data from MCC’s databases to cloud-hosted solutions.  COTS products can be proposed as solutions for customer requirements. Specifics will be  included in each new development task."
        },
        {
          "sourceKey": "mcc-issued-pws-text",
          "locator": "word/document.xml B271; PWS 4.2.2.3.1",
          "excerpt": "Although an another contract provides general infrastructure support, the Contractor shall provide database administration expertise in connection with the applications they develop and support. This includes, but is not limited to, database architecture design and implementation, dataset normalization, data migration support, data management application creation, troubleshooting data and structure issues, data recovery, building indexes, load balancing, backup and restore services, database and application tuning, and assisting with the infrastructure DBAs (Database Administrators) as needed as an expert. Current database standards are MS SQL Server (enterprise) and MySQL. Additional database platforms may be required to support cloud application development."
        },
        {
          "sourceKey": "mcc-issued-pws-text",
          "locator": "word/document.xml B277; PWS 4.2.3",
          "excerpt": "The Contractor shall be required to work jointly with MCC’s operations and security vendors to maintain a DevSecOps culture that removes silos between teams, incorporates security throughout the development process, and promotes continuous improvement and automation. MCC has a CI/CD pipeline that automates deployments. MCC expects to continue enhance the pipeline by incorporating automated unit testing, and adding robust, automated system monitoring. Additionally, the Contractor shall jointly with MCC’s operations and security vendors, be responsible for the iterative configuration of the CI/CD pipeline and its on-going maintenance. "
        },
        {
          "sourceKey": "mcc-issued-pws-text",
          "locator": "word/document.xml B319; PWS 4.5",
          "excerpt": "This requirement is optional and shall be utilized if deemed necessary during the life of the contract. The Contractor shall provide the total costs of non-labor tools per year to the Government."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "15",
      "decision": "partial",
      "owner": "Contracts lead and delivery architect",
      "response": "Proposed feedback: a single-award BPA with service-area orders can give MCC a common accountability and architecture model while allowing different work packages to be scheduled and priced. Its practical design should make shared dependencies, release ownership and service boundaries explicit so orders do not duplicate management or leave integration work unowned. Define a service catalog, transparent labor/other-cost treatment, acceptance and change rules, and a repeatable approach to pricing fixed outcomes and temporary surge work. Review the risks of dependence on one provider, constrained specialist access, weak price comparisons after award and difficult transition. Address them through current handover artifacts, portable source/configuration/data, explicit transition responsibilities, measurable order-level performance and permitted specialist teaming. Compare the contemplated structure with alternatives against coordination cost, competition, specialist coverage and continuity, using the agency’s actual acquisition constraints.",
      "reviewNote": "Proposed market-research feedback for RFI 15, L125, coordinated with rows 3 and 5.a. The company contracts owner must review eligibility, vehicle terms and pricing implications with the actual contemplated acquisition documents. This is a design comparison for MCC’s consideration, not a claim that a particular contract structure has been selected or is legally available.",
      "responseDisposition": "answer",
      "status": "in_progress",
      "issuedEvidence": [
        {
